nge in the world and that we can  figure things out nothing is set in  stone and each of us sort of has the  ability and the creativity to make those  changes I know some people even some  friends of mine from school who had  parents who were sort of quite academic  and they actually did actively put  effort into trying to make their kids  pursue science or any other particular  topic whether it's medicine or law as  well and actually those people that I  know didn't end up pursuing what their  parents wanted them to in the end so you  know I actually think the essence here  is to not try too hard if you're trying  to actively force someone to have an  interest in something it would probably  backfire and the opposite would be true  I even think you know some of those  efforts could be detrimental in terms of  science and the way like maybe if I had  been more exposed to like little science  experiments that they make for kids and  I see selling in stores now maybe I  would have had a skewed idea that  science is just mixing chemicals and  making a volcano like a baking soda  volcano maybe I would have thought more  that science was just that stereotypical  white lab coat mixing things and seeing  action happen from that because to me I  don't really find those sort of science  experiments interesting and I never did  I never found the baking soda volcano  interesting at all the only science ever  found interesting was the very abstract  ideas the maths and the physics and  cosmology and things like that so I'm  sort of glad I wasn't exposed to any  particular stereotype of science that  had been you know generically made for  kids because I was able to jump straight  to some of that more advanced science  and think actually this is really cool  I'm glad I'm just meeting it in this  natural awesome form so those are sort  of my thoughts I hope they make sense in  essence if you're trying to make someone  be interested in science don't try too  hard  you can't mold people to be what you  want them to be and if you know someone  that you want to be like more curious or  something like that just encourage them  in a way that makes them feel that  anything is possible that they can  explore things and that they are capable  of researching ideas because they don't  need to just believe what other people  tell them they can go out and find  evidence and find facts for themselves
 

